# CCE PR cloud entitlement review (change-control / pre-deploy IAM)

After **check-info-and-clone** succeeds and `repo_clone_path` is set, run inside **one Ubuntu execute_series** (single `$` only):

1. Ensure CCE pack: `mkdir -p "$CCE_PACK_DIR" && echo "$CCE_PACK_B64" | base64 -d | tar -xz -C "$(dirname "$CCE_PACK_DIR")" 2>/dev/null || true`
2. `export WORK_ROOT="$(dirname "$repo_clone_path")"` (or workflow WORK_ROOT from notes)
3. PR delta (default base `origin/main` or `default_branch` from notes):

```bash
bash "$CCE_PACK_DIR/cce-pr-delta.sh" delta "$repo_clone_path" "$${default_branch:-origin/main}" HEAD "$WORK_ROOT"
```

4. `note` keys: `cce_pr_delta_path`, `cce_new_entitlement_count`, `cce_scan_status` (from jq `.scan_status`).
5. If `new_entitlement_count > 0`, include top 5 `new_entitlements` in the **create-pr-comment** or validation stage summary for IAM/CAB review.

Skip when `SKIP_CCE=1`. Built-in cloud mapper only (no custom lens required).
